hat of a 30-year-old woman: fuller, slightly husky and a notch lower in pitch. The voice sounds like it's coming from a close podcast mic with little echo and reverberation. As her mouth moves away from the microphone, the audio changes in volume. Soft room tone of a small podcast studio, close-mic'd podcast sound.\",\n      \"referencias\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 7, \"tipo\": \"H\", \"habla\": \"B\", \"duracion\": 8, \"frame_inicial\": \"host-b\",\n      \"lineas\": [\n        { \"orden\": 10, \"texto\": \"Nada que ver, a mí no me pasó.\" },\n        { \"orden\": 11, \"texto\": \"Eso era lo que me daba miedo también.\" }\n      ],\n      \"linea\": \"Nada que ver, a mí no me pasó. Eso era lo que me daba miedo también.\",\n      \"prompt_imagen_inicial\": null, \"prompt_imagen_final\": null,\n      \"prompt_video\": \"Podcast-style video. Static camera, medium close-up framing locked to the start frame throughout. She speaks directly to someone off-camera, delivering multiple lines with natural pauses between them as if listening to responses.\\n\\nNo captions. No background music. No camera movement or angle changes.\\n\\nShe says each line exactly as written, only once, without repeating, adding or changing any word, and without \\\"um\\\", \\\"uh\\\" or \\\"eh\\\" that are not in the script. After her last line she says nothing else: she stays silent, listening, until the clip ends.\\n\\nSCRIPT:\\n\\nLínea 1: \\\"Nada que ver, a mí no me pasó.\\\"\\nDelivery: she only says her own lines, never the other person's questions or comments, and between lines stays silent, listening; she shakes her head calmly with a relaxed smile and reaches one hand out toward her friend off-camera, as if touching her arm to reassure her\\n\\nLínea 2: \\\"Eso era lo que me daba miedo también.\\\"\\nDelivery: honest and close, her hand comes back to her chest, a small nod\\n\\nAudio: she speaks in a natural everyday Colombian Spanish accent (not neutral Latin American, not Mex