 out a short sigh just before saying it, half laughing at herself; the word pa' is the short spoken form of 'para', said simply as 'pa'\\n\\nAudio: she speaks in a natural everyday Colombian Spanish accent (not neutral Latin American, not Mexican, not from Spain) at a quick, animated conversational pace, confessional and self-deprecating, laughing at herself. Her voice is that of a 27-year-old woman: bright, light and medium-high in pitch, full of energy. The voice sounds like it's coming from a close podcast mic with little echo and reverberation. As her mouth moves away from the microphone, the audio changes in volume. Soft room tone of a small podcast studio, close-mic'd podcast sound.\",\n      \"referencias\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"n\": 2, \"tipo\": \"H\", \"habla\": \"A\", \"duracion\": 10, \"frame_inicial\": \"host-a\",\n      \"lineas\": [\n        { \"orden\": 6, \"texto\": \"¿Y qué te tomaste?\" },\n        { \"orden\": 9, \"texto\": \"¿Y eso no engorda? Porque yo probé unas pastillas y me dio rebote.\" },\n        { \"orden\": 12, \"texto\": \"¿Y cómo te fue?\" }\n      ],\n      \"linea\": \"¿Y qué te tomaste? ¿Y eso no engorda? Porque yo probé unas pastillas y me dio rebote. ¿Y cómo te fue?\",\n      \"prompt_imagen_inicial\": null, \"prompt_imagen_final\": null,\n      \"prompt_video\": \"Podcast-style video. Static camera, medium close-up framing locked to the start frame throughout. She speaks directly to someone off-camera, delivering multiple lines with natural pauses between them as if listening to responses.\\n\\nNo captions. No background music. No camera movement or angle changes.\\n\\nShe says each line exactly as written, only once, without repeating, adding or changing any word, and without \\\"um\\\", \\\"uh\\\" or \\\"eh\\\" that are not in the script. After her last line she says nothing else: she stays silent, listening, until the clip ends.\\n\\nSCRIPT:\\n\\nLínea 1: \\\"¿Y qué te tomaste?\\\"\\nDelivery: she only says her own line